    "id": "ACT-GRAM",
    "revision": 7,
    "title": "Count occasions and complete passes",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-event-counts-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Count occasions and complete passes",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Put an event count after the action. 次 counts separate occasions; 遍 counts complete passes through the relevant material or activity. In the example about a familiar book, two 遍 means going through the whole book twice, not merely opening it on two occasions.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我去了两次。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ qù le liǎng cì 。",
                "meaning": "I went twice, on two occasions.",
                "audio": "9eef70debd6ffca1950905beda8f0f4c8ecdd74dc28b2c3499ae7ca8c6013c3d"
              },
              {
                "text": "我看了两遍。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ kàn le liǎng biàn 。",
                "meaning": "I went through it twice from beginning to end.",
                "audio": "0b8a8df64c42ed12cfbad7186692001286cb96e7e76bdb6a7925be242be86648"
              },
              {
                "text": "请再说一遍。",
                "pinyin": "qǐng zài shuō yī biàn 。",
                "meaning": "Please say the whole thing once more.",
                "audio": "6e5999465f9bcb083be6811e4d2b3b24ad68c2e80a4ca195e366c74729ea2787"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "次",
                "pinyin": "cì",
                "meaning": "measure word for occasions",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "80398c2eda1112b2d8bd088b17850b7c6c9f3950ed955547755b4e279096e8a7"
              },
              {
